WEBVTT

00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:05.700
I'll tell you what I've deduced.

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:13.040
It appears to me that somehow you guys are detecting the intent to kill

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:15.750
and using that to catch the killer.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:20.330
I gather you have a murderer cooperate
in your peculiar investigation, don't you?

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:25.410
The reason the gloomy guy from the next cell over

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:31.290
was able to get the murderer in the
opposite cell to kill himself the other night

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:37.000
after a single conversation, was that he
knew secrets from deep in the man's mind.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:42.450
Practically every day, this Narihisago
character is taken away by the guards

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:47.290
and returns looking like a new layer of
despair has been applied to his dreary face.

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:51.950
That doesn't happen from an
interrogation about your own crime.

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:58.080
As he whispered that night, it
was like he was silently screaming.

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:01.200
I wish you guys could have heard it, too.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:04.750
Lucky guess? No, of course not.

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:08.410
It appears Fukuda's IQ exceeded 150.

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:12.290
No telling what it is with
the hole in his brain, though.

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:15.200
But, sir!

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.830
He's a suspect, and we still
haven't found his last victim!

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:20.830
I read the report.

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:24.450
However, with Narihisago
in solitary confinement,

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:27.580
the entire organization is at a standstill.

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:37.450
This is Kaeru.

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:40.290
And I am Anaido.

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:45.160
I don't know my full name.
But I'm the brilliant detective.

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:46.950
Anaido has died.

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:48.700
This well was a failure, too.

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:52.290
He's tried seven wells ten
times each in three days, but...

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:54.750
His time of operation is far too short.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:57.410
It just strains the pilot unnecessarily.

00:01:57.410 --> 00:01:59.700
He won't make a suitable substitute.

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:02.040
For now just extract him.

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:05.450
All Narihisago does is kill serial killers.

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:08.910
Perhaps <i>our </i>performance is poor,

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:14.080
due to our unavoidable resistance
to working with a <i>real </i>serial killer.

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:16.330
That's no excuse.

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:20.330
Even so, he simply dies too much.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:26.830
Apparently, the sort of person who would drill a hole in their head themselves

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:30.000
has remarkably little survival ability.

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:30.540
This is that Gravedigger thing.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:32.120
For real?

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:41.870
I've been captured by the Gravedigger,

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:45.080
and people all over the world are watching, huh.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:50.660
Everyone who came to see me die,
sorry to disappoint you!

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:54.450
I'm going to live! You'll see!

00:04:54.450 --> 00:04:55.620
You'll see!

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:57.950
Until someone comes to save me,

00:04:57.950 --> 00:04:59.500
I'll hang on!

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:05.910
Shoot! Can't waste it.

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:11.450
Was it 52 hours?
The record for the longest survivor.

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:14.540
I'll do my best to smash that record!

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:18.200
So somebody please come find me!

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:22.160
This is the seventh victim the Gravedigger has buried alive,

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:25.870
yet the Japanese police have no leads.

00:05:25.870 --> 00:05:30.120
Be that as it may, I don't believe
anyone besides the investigators

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:35.700
should watch the Gravedigger's broadcasts,
no matter how curious they are.

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:39.660
According to experts, the signal is
traveling through multiple foreign servers,

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:42.580
making the source difficult to locate.

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:49.580
To continuously film the victim's
suffering--it's essentially a snuff film.

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:56.000
Good morning.

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:59.620
Sorry!

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:02.250
Get off your high horse.

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:06.830
I didn't mean to sound superior.
Forgive my rudeness.

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:10.620
You're right. This is work.
You didn't need an apology.

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:15.580
Now, is this where Kikuchi Keiko was kidnapped?

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:19.000
Yes. Looks like she was
taken on her way to school.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:21.410
Her phone was left behind.

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:26.080
Work? This is a Gravedigger crime scene.
Won't you people be useless?

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:27.000
Hey!

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.830
Stop antagonizing the Kura kid.

00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:32.290
The Kura has a dedicated unit

00:06:32.290 --> 00:06:36.700
searching every part of the city top to bottom for Gravedigger victims.

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:41.040
The entire police force is doing its part.

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:46.620
The Kura hasn't been operating
lately, though. You're slacking off.

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:48.580
Whoa! Success!

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:49.750
Finally got something!

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:51.000
Maybe it's a sign.

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:52.450
Thanks a lot!

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:55.120
Cognition particles have been gleaned.

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:56.620
We can construct a well.

00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:59.000
That's the first time in this case.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:01.330
Let Narihisago out of solitary.

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:11.290
Hey, partner.

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:38.040
This corpse has been
burnt to a crisp, face and all.

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:40.830
But I know exactly who it is.

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:42.750
This is Kaeru.

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:45.700
And I am Sakaido, the brilliant detective.

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:49.450
I will solve the mystery
of Kaeru's death without fail.

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:57.160
I don't see any wounds.

00:07:57.160 --> 00:08:04.750
Though, with the body burnt so thoroughly,
light cuts or punctures might not show.

00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:37.620
Horrible.

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:43.910
How would Kaeru burn
to death in a room with no fire?

00:08:50.370 --> 00:08:51.790
What?

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:56.910
A girl?

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:03.330
Sakaido has died.

00:09:03.330 --> 00:09:04.370
Extract him.

00:09:04.370 --> 00:09:06.450
Then put him right back in.

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:20.000
Looks like I'm still good on air.

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:22.830
It's tough not having any food.

00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:24.870
Though, it's even tougher that.

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:28.120
I have no idea what time it is right now.

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:30.000
It seems like it's been a while.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.910
I wonder whether it's been 24 hours.

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:43.500
What's that?

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:53.790
All right! He survived!

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:56.870
Kaeru!

00:09:56.870 --> 00:10:01.330
It's pointless. Kaeru is already dead.

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:02.580
There you go!

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:05.330
Our job is not to cheer for Sakaido.

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:06.790
Sorry.

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:11.500
Well, we do need Sakaido to live
in order to get more information.

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:15.370
The only thing we know is that the girl
Sakaido discovered on the top floor

00:10:15.370 --> 00:10:19.830
is the victim, Kikuchi Keiko,
when she was ten years old.

00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:25.910
Neither this victim nor the Gravedigger's
other victims were burned to death.

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:30.410
Maybe the fire isn't actually fire
and symbolizes something else.

00:10:30.410 --> 00:10:33.000
Could that be it?

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:34.950
Oh, not again.

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:47.870
That's the third backdraft death.

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:50.700
Extract Sakaido then re-inject immediately.

00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:54.160
He's been dying in the well
for more than six hours straight.

00:10:54.160 --> 00:10:55.830
He must be near exhaustion.

00:10:55.830 --> 00:10:58.290
He got plenty of rest in solitary.

00:10:58.290 --> 00:10:59.700
Inject him.

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:02.830
Yes, sir.

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:15.620
Incredible. He doesn't remember the previous runs, right?

00:11:15.620 --> 00:11:19.620
Yeah. It's thanks to Sakaido's ability as a brilliant detective.

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:22.660
But there's still a long way to go.

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:35.950
Sit tight! I'm coming to save you!

00:11:43.290 --> 00:11:45.790
Do you need a break, Narihisago?

00:11:45.790 --> 00:11:47.950
I used the bathroom a long time ago.

00:11:47.950 --> 00:11:51.870
The seat's a bit dirty, but I'm fine.

00:11:51.870 --> 00:11:53.910
I see.

00:11:53.910 --> 00:11:55.370
Inject him.

00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:07.160
Sakaido has died.

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:08.450
The same spot again?

00:12:08.450 --> 00:12:10.200
Extract him.

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:13.330
Before you re-inject him, let him eat.

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:17.040
Yes, sir. We'll also clean
the cockpit in the meantime.

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:22.750
We don't know what effect Narihisago's
environment has on Sakaido's performance.

00:12:22.750 --> 00:12:23.580
Please do.

00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:28.200
No one's come for me... Why wouldn't...

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:31.910
Hey, wouldn't cognition
particles have been found

00:12:31.910 --> 00:12:36.000
in any of the Gravedigger's first six cases?

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:40.700
Well, the victims are still buried
somewhere and haven't been found.

00:12:40.700 --> 00:12:42.790
Even though we can't scan the bodies,

00:12:42.790 --> 00:12:47.290
the Gravedigger's drive to kill should
be clear at the point of kidnapping.

00:12:47.290 --> 00:12:51.750
True. But cognition particles
can even blow away in the wind,

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:55.160
so they might have just dispersed
if there was a minuscule amount.

00:12:55.160 --> 00:12:58.790
Someone who buried <i>six </i>people
alive has a trivial drive to kill?

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:00.370
I find that hard to believe.

00:13:00.370 --> 00:13:04.120
Besides, the killer livestreamed the victim's deaths,

00:13:04.120 --> 00:13:07.330
prolonged the stream by leaving oxygen canisters,

00:13:07.330 --> 00:13:11.870
and then showed their corpses decaying after they died.

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:16.450
Someone so sadistic couldn't
possibly have a weak drive to kill.

00:13:16.450 --> 00:13:19.620
Cognition particles ought to remain.

00:13:19.620 --> 00:13:21.830
Well, we found some this time,

00:13:21.830 --> 00:13:24.830
so catching the killer will clear all that up.

00:13:24.830 --> 00:13:29.330
My point is, why did we find any this time?

00:13:42.910 --> 00:13:45.120
I want to save that girl.

00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:48.040
But that isn't my task.

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:52.540
My job is to elucidate the
mystery of Kaeru's death.

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:58.450
How was Kaeru rendered
a burnt corpse in a place with no fire?

00:14:02.830 --> 00:14:04.330
Sakaido has died.

00:14:04.330 --> 00:14:07.830
Extract him. Let Narihisago
have a five-minute break.

00:14:07.830 --> 00:14:09.410
Understood.

00:14:10.830 --> 00:14:13.870
You should all rest as well.

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:16.160
No, it's not a problem.

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:18.830
It <i>is </i>a problem.

00:14:18.830 --> 00:14:22.250
There are things with which
tired brains cannot contend.

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:26.950
Kikuchi Keiko has little time left.
We can go without for two nights.

00:14:26.950 --> 00:14:28.910
Narihisago will be fine, too.

00:14:28.910 --> 00:14:32.660
Certainly, Narihisago the
police officer would be.

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:37.120
However, these days we have
Narihisago Akihito the serial killer.

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:40.500
Your time as colleagues has long since passed.

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:45.370
The desire to save people
may no longer motivate him.

00:15:04.830 --> 00:15:06.080
He did it!

00:15:59.660 --> 00:16:01.250
Sorry for the wait.

00:16:02.830 --> 00:16:04.330
All right!

00:16:10.330 --> 00:16:13.450
You were scared, huh. It's all right now.

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:17.450
This place is on fire and full of dead people.

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:19.660
It's exactly as she says.

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:23.870
This building is on fire,
and littered with burnt bodies.

00:16:23.870 --> 00:16:27.080
This girl is the only soul I've seen alive.

00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:29.790
Everyone else had already burned to death.

00:16:32.040 --> 00:16:36.250
Kaeru is the X factor here after all.

00:16:36.250 --> 00:16:40.410
Only Kaeru was in a place with no fire.

00:16:40.410 --> 00:16:44.290
In other words, Kaeru didn't die in this fire.

00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:48.250
She was burned elsewhere and then moved here.

00:16:48.250 --> 00:16:50.250
For what purpose?

00:16:50.250 --> 00:16:54.500
Her killer tried to hide her
among the bodies in this giant fire.

00:16:54.500 --> 00:16:56.830
The killer tried to use this major fire

00:16:56.830 --> 00:17:00.450
to cover up the fact that she died in a different one.

00:17:00.450 --> 00:17:02.910
It's Gilbert Keith Chesterton!

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:07.700
A wise man hides a leaf in the forest.
So hide a corpse in a hill of corpses.

00:17:07.700 --> 00:17:09.790
The Gravedigger didn't do this!

00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:11.000
It's a copycat!

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:15.080
They tried to hide their murder
in the Gravedigger's serial murder.

00:17:15.080 --> 00:17:17.870
That's why we found cognition particles!

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:20.080
Then who actually did it?

00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:24.160
Thanks. You helped me solve the mystery!

00:17:24.160 --> 00:17:25.830
What do you mean?

00:17:25.830 --> 00:17:27.580
Don't worry about it.

00:17:27.580 --> 00:17:29.660
Come on. Let's get out of here.

00:17:29.660 --> 00:17:30.660
Okay!

00:17:30.660 --> 00:17:32.290
But how?

00:17:32.290 --> 00:17:37.330
Hmm. Well, just trust me.
I'm the brilliant detective.

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:44.830
Look! Mr. Oono's house is really, really on fire.

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:47.370
What did she say?

00:17:47.370 --> 00:17:49.750
See, Mr. Oono is a failure,

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:53.450
so to start all over again, he lit his house on fire.

00:17:53.450 --> 00:17:56.620
Even though his family was sleeping.

00:17:56.620 --> 00:18:00.580
He probably thinks I was watching him.

00:18:00.580 --> 00:18:02.000
Suspect found.

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:07.000
A Oono Genpei lived in Kikuchi Keiko's
neighborhood until she was five.

00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:08.450
The face matches, too.

00:18:08.450 --> 00:18:09.830
Let's go, Hondomachi.

00:18:09.830 --> 00:18:11.000
Yes, sir!

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:20.120
Freeze!

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:21.910
Hands up! On your knees!

00:18:21.910 --> 00:18:22.910
Suspect secured!

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:24.410
Victim not found.

00:18:24.410 --> 00:18:26.660
Where is Kikuchi Keiko? Tell us!

00:18:26.660 --> 00:18:29.620
That mass-produced rug...

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:34.250
Check under the rug!

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:35.410
Roger!

00:18:38.120 --> 00:18:40.700
There's another room! Check it! Hurry!

00:18:40.700 --> 00:18:42.410
Where's the medical unit?

00:18:46.580 --> 00:18:48.410
She's still alive!

00:18:48.410 --> 00:18:50.700
We're gonna make it!

00:18:53.330 --> 00:18:55.500
What's wrong?

00:18:55.500 --> 00:18:57.700
It's not live at all.

00:18:57.700 --> 00:18:59.040
Look.

00:18:59.040 --> 00:19:02.290
The victim's barrel is still nailed shut.

00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:05.040
It's a recording.

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:07.410
The cell phone was a trick.

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:09.540
The victim is dead.

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:11.620
Appears to have been several days.

00:19:11.620 --> 00:19:15.040
Dammit! You monster!

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:19.410
I don't remember Mr. Oono.

00:19:19.410 --> 00:19:22.870
I kept telling him I didn't see anything.

00:19:22.870 --> 00:19:25.250
He burned it all out of frustration.

00:19:25.250 --> 00:19:27.950
Cause Mr. Oono is a failure.

00:19:27.950 --> 00:19:31.450
But you're safe now. I'm here.

00:19:31.450 --> 00:19:33.160
Come on. Let's go.

00:19:44.830 --> 00:19:46.580
What's wrong?

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:50.330
You shouldn't have to see any more scary things.

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:52.830
Thank you for coming to save me.

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:56.410
Thanks for helping me reach the truth.

00:19:56.410 --> 00:20:00.540
Hey, mister, will you tell me your name?

00:20:01.870 --> 00:20:04.620
We got the guy.

00:20:04.620 --> 00:20:06.250
I see.

00:20:06.250 --> 00:20:12.040
Since the victim knew him...
and he left cognition particles behind...

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:14.040
Was he actually the Gravedigger?

00:20:14.040 --> 00:20:16.000
Unfortunately not.

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:19.250
A copycat, then. Hide a leaf in the forest.

00:20:19.250 --> 00:20:20.120
Yeah.

00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:22.870
Did you find the victim in time?

00:20:22.870 --> 00:20:24.790
It was too late.

00:20:24.790 --> 00:20:27.790
The broadcast was actually recorded video.

00:20:27.790 --> 00:20:30.200
So it was all for nothing.

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:37.410
Do you want to kill him, Narihisago?

00:20:37.410 --> 00:20:38.620
Can I?

00:20:38.620 --> 00:20:41.450
I'm asking whether you <i>want </i>to.

00:20:43.290 --> 00:20:45.700
You--
Momoki.

00:20:45.700 --> 00:20:52.750
While I've been at the Kura,
I've kill--driven five people to suicide.

00:20:52.750 --> 00:20:57.500
True, I killed them all, of my
own will, acting on my own urges.

00:20:57.500 --> 00:21:02.080
But, Momoki I didn't
particularly want to kill them.

00:21:02.080 --> 00:21:05.410
I didn't have any malice toward them.

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:10.080
This overwhelming urge to kill just welled up inside me,

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:12.580
and that's when it occurred to me:

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:14.910
I could kill this person.

00:21:14.910 --> 00:21:18.700
And so I did. I had no real reason.

00:21:18.700 --> 00:21:20.580
So, now what?

00:21:20.580 --> 00:21:23.250
Are you just going to keep killing?

00:21:23.250 --> 00:21:24.700
No.

00:21:24.700 --> 00:21:28.580
People--assuming I'm still a person, that is--

00:21:28.580 --> 00:21:32.000
people don't decide to act
based on their impulse alone.

00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:34.750
You <i>are </i>a person, Narihisago.

00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:37.000
I guarantee it.

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:39.200
You're just weak as a person.

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:42.080
Just one more thing.

00:21:44.250 --> 00:21:47.870
Do you still consider me a friend?

00:21:51.580 --> 00:21:58.160
That's probably the lifeline that
ultimately tethers me to reason.

00:22:04.450 --> 00:22:06.620
That was one hell of an outcome.

00:22:06.620 --> 00:22:09.950
This means the Gravedigger is still out there.

00:22:09.950 --> 00:22:12.200
And we still have no leads.

00:22:12.200 --> 00:22:16.000
Well, yeah. Nevertheless, that
investigation can resume tomorrow.

00:22:16.000 --> 00:22:19.160
It's early, but let's close up shop for today.

00:22:28.160 --> 00:22:29.790
I recognize him.

00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:49.790
Oh, well.

00:22:52.450 --> 00:22:53.910
You're...

00:22:55.580 --> 00:22:57.080
Mr. Kazuta!

00:22:57.080 --> 00:23:00.200
Mr. Kazuta Haruka right? The missing person.

00:23:00.200 --> 00:23:02.950
You're alive! That's great!
